# A token has a name (CR 111.4: a token created with no name given is named for its subtypes plus "Token", here "Goblin Token"), so a Goblin token from Dragon Fodder can block Pompous Gadabout (CR 509.1b, 201.2): only a creature with no name cannot.

[Bot1 Deck]
Pompous Gadabout
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Dragon Fodder
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Pompous Gadabout.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Dragon Fodder.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Pompous Gadabout > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Goblin Token#1 > Pompous Gadabout)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Pompous Gadabout.Damage = 1
